949,0.02121891,-0.01588168,0.05427826,0.01517478,-0.00380422,0.09375113,0.06355148,-0.00960074,-0.01295451,0.00090094,0.11053395,0.03632389,-0.01082824,0.02695931,-0.0494321,0.01976356,0.01971729,-0.03281868,0.01042536,0.00169915,0.07340409,0.02509665,0.09689741,0.03550054,0.00846345,0.04588643,0.03899442,0.01180366,0.07837623,-0.02937929,-0.02071122,0.06981106,0.08533723,-0.03477281,-0.06851998,-0.01593789,-0.05082651,0.03134634,-0.02813997,0.0092283,0.06693524,0.01606639,0.03580472,-0.01892398,-0.06283673,0.02945852,0.01727364,0.01540405,-0.01733453,0.01183728,-0.03450118,0.04034278,-0.00259612],"last_embed":{"hash":"zokyrw","tokens":502}}},"last_read":{"hash":"zokyrw","at":1778088457616},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1778088443317,"size":33627,"at":1778088456917,"hash":"zokyrw"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,13],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting":[14,222],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{1}":[16,16],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{2}":[17,17],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{3}":[18,18],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{4}":[19,19],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{5}":[20,21],"##How a housewife from Queens 'took the L out of flab' when she lost 72 pounds and founded Weight Watchers - and inspired an author to examine her 'tortured' relationship with dieting#{6}":[22,222]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Beslenmenin Psikososyal Yönleri","target":"Beslenmenin Psikososyal Yönleri","line":10},{"title":"Dersler/Diyet İlkeleri ve Popüler Diyetler","target":"Dersler/Diyet İlkeleri ve Popüler Diyetler","line":10},{"title":"Popüler Diyetler","target":"Popüler Diyetler","line":10},{"title":"wrote","target":"https://clicks.trx-hub.com/xid/mailonline_8bcce_mailonline?q=https%3A%2F%2Ffave.co%2F36nMApc&p=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailymail.co.uk%2Fnews%2Farticle-8341577%2FHow-Jean-Nidetch-housewife-Queens-lost-72-pounds-founded-Weight-Watchers.html&event_type=click&trafficsource=web&device=desktop&ref=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F&articleid=8341577","line":28},{"title":"Jean Nidetch, was an overweight housewife living in Queens with an addiction to Mallomar cookies and a compulsive eating habit. Her weight fluctuated her entire life, but she finally decided to loose weight after running into a neighbor at the supermarket who mistook her for being pregnant","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/21/22/28636466-8341577-image-a-1_1590098337280.jpg","line":30,"embedded":true},{"title":"In 1961, Jean entered an obesity clinic where she lost 72 pounds from the strict diet. She began hosting friends in casual meet-ups to share dieting tips she that learned in the program, in an early version of Weight Watchers. Within two months, six people turned into forty, which turned into a hundred and Jean had to host the weekly meetings in the basement of her apartment building","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/21/23/28636268-8341577-image-a-7_1590100016600.jpg","line":34,"embedded":true},{"title":"By 1963, Jean's casual group meetings had become so popular that she took her show on the road. She partnered with Felice and Albert Lippert who helped turn it into a proper business charging dieters a $3 fee to attend the weekly meetings. In May, 1963, they officially formed a corporation and called it Weight Watchers International","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/14/28636488-8341577-image-a-7_1590155516798.jpg","line":38,"embedded":true},{"title":"Jean Nidetch  grew up in a working class, Jewish household in Brooklyn during the Depression, but for as long as she could remember, Jean said she felt shame for being overweight. 'I wanted to be the pretty one. A fat kid never hears the words pretty, adorable, cute, handsome. Instead they’re always good, honest, neat, clean, trustworthy'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/21/23/28636254-8341577-image-a-8_1590100038764.jpg","line":42,"embedded":true},{"title":"After a lifetime of yo-yo dieting, NYC writer Marisa Meltzer was hoping to put a face to her problems when she came across Jean Nidetch's obituary in 2015. Instead, she said: 'I didn't see a villain...I saw myself.' Meltzer's book (available now) chronicles Nidetch's life story with her own personal weight loss journey","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/14/28636298-8341577-image-a-3_1590153414201.jpg","line":50,"embedded":true},{"title":"Jean Nidetch poses for a before and after portrait which she always carried with her to show off her weight loss success. Though Jean got rid of all her large clothes, she kept one dress to serve as a reminder of her former self - this later became a requirement of Weight Watchers leaders","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/13/28636250-8341577-image-a-1_1590150412460.jpg","line":68,"embedded":true},{"title":"Jean Nidetch, founder of Weight watchers, wears a bathing suit on the beach in 1946. Marisa Meltzer writes: 'When I look at old photos of her before she lost the weight, the physical resemblance between us is so strong, she could easily be my aunt or cousin; she could almost be me somehow transported back in time to New York City in 1961'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/14/28636300-8341577-image-a-4_1590154972499.jpg","line":72,"embedded":true},{"title":"After her dramatic 72 pound weight loss, Jean celebrated with a complete makeover by dying her hair platinum blonde, a color that she kept until her dying day. Jean (pictured above in 1988) wrote in her autobiography: 'It’s not any more inconvenient to work on the size of you than it is to work on changing your hair color. I’m not thrilled about going for the touch ups, you know. I do it because I like the result'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/14/28636274-8341577-image-a-5_1590155008961.jpg","line":76,"embedded":true},{"title":"Marisa Meltzer (above) explores the parallels between her personal struggle with weight and Jean Nidetch's life story in This Is Big. The result is a touching and candid memoir/ biography, she said: 'For the past several years I have felt trapped between dieting my way to a slimmer body and simply giving up and trying to love myself as is, caught between change and acceptance'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/15/28636296-8341577-image-a-13_1590158305127.jpg","line":84,"embedded":true},{"title":"Marisa Meltzer poses with Busy Philipps. As a journalist who covers beauty, wellness, fashion and celebrity, Marisa said that she feels like she 'lives in a world of thin people.' And adds: 'Sometimes I think my size is an asset to my job, that it's easier for the most beautiful and famous women to relax and open up to someone they don't perceive as a threat'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/17/28713086-8341577-image-m-23_1590166643829.jpg","line":102,"embedded":true},{"title":"Marisa poses with her beloved bulldog, Joan. She recalled a time when two teenager girls doted over Joan's chubby physique. She said, 'We all just accept dogs for showing up. I wish I could do that for myself'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/18/28713060-8341577-image-m-25_1590166811560.jpg","line":106,"embedded":true},{"title":"400 people attended the first official Weight Watchers meeting. Jean loved the spotlight and Meltzer said, she 'possessed of an almost mythical relatability among her followers'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/14/28636484-8341577-image-a-6_1590155477373.jpg","line":120,"embedded":true},{"title":"Weight Watchers founder Jean Nidetch posing alongside photo of herself weighing over 100 pounds more than she does now.  (Photo by Martha Holmes/The LIFE Images Collection via Getty Images/Getty Images)","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/15/28636244-8341577-image-a-9_1590156892430.jpg","line":124,"embedded":true},{"title":"'The newspaper columnist Brady compared Jean to the Pied Piper, a nightclub entertainer, and a revival preacher,' wrote Marisa Meltzer. It wasn't long before she became a weight-loss celebrity greeted by zealous fans carrying signs such as: 'BE LEAN WITH JEAN,' or 'HIPS HIPS AWAY' and 'IF YOU INDULGE, YOU'RE GONNA BULGE'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/15/28636482-8341577-image-a-8_1590156864563.jpg","line":128,"embedded":true},{"title":"Weight Watchers turned into a massive cottage industry with a restaurant, frozen food line, cookbook and magazine. Above, Jean demonstrates a few of the new low calorie products. Meltzer said Jean was a pioneer in the wellness and lifestyle industries, paving the way for future entrepreneurs like Martha Stewart, Ina Garten and Gwyneth Paltrow. 'The problem for Jean with being a pioneer was that her fame was so new and original that the powers that be at the time didn’t seem to quite know what to do with her'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/17/28636246-8341577-image-m-21_1590163812175.jpg","line":150,"embedded":true},{"title":"Jean wasn't one to mince words 'and would ask her audience why they made things so hard on themselves, if they’d rather waste food or waste themselves. She liked to call out members by name like a schoolmarm and ask them point-blank to describe their biggest food weakness,' wrote Marisa in her biography This Is Big","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/15/28636476-8341577-image-a-11_1590157366853.jpg","line":154,"embedded":true},{"title":"Jean Nidetch, meets with guests at a Weight Watchers meeting in Louisville, Kentucky. The meetups were centered around dieting tips, where Jean would re-tell her own story and moderate a conversation among attendees. She would end every meeting with: 'If you leave here to have coffee and melon, coffee and fresh fruit cup…I wish you well. But if you're leaving here to have coffee and a Danish, I affectionately wish you heartburn'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/15/28636494-8341577-image-a-10_1590157209602.jpg","line":158,"embedded":true},{"title":"Marisa Meltzer (right) attends the London Review of Books 30th Anniversary Party in 2010. She writes: 'Activists say fat isn’t something to be apologized for, but I’ve felt sorry about it my whole life. I believe I deserve equality and justice, but I’m not sure that the fight to demand it is any easier than the fight to earn it'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/18/28713076-8341577-image-a-27_1590167297189.jpg","line":176,"embedded":true},{"title":"'My fantasy for my body is to be whatever size it is and for no one to see me as fat; for the social perception of fatness to cease to exist. I think it’s less about a hatred of fat people or my body and more about wanting to be able to live in a way where I am noticed for what I choose'","target":"https://i.dailymail.co.uk/1s/2020/05/22/18/28713080-8341577-image-m-28_1590167306937.jpg","line":180,"embedded":true},{"title":"This Is Big,","target":"https://clicks.trx-hub.com/xid/mailonline_8bcce_mailonline?q=https%3A%2F%2Ffave.co%2F36nMApc&p=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailymail.co.uk%2Fnews%2Farticle-8341577%2FHow-Jean-Nidetch-housewife-Queens-lost-72-pounds-founded-Weight-Watchers.html&event_type=click&trafficsource=web&device=desktop&ref=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F&articleid=8341577","line":206}],"metadata":{"title":"Be lean with Jean: How a housewife from Queens founded Weight Watchers","source":"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-8341577/How-Jean-Nidetch-housewife-Queens-lost-72-pounds-founded-Weight-Watchers.html","author":null,"published":"2020-05-22","created":"2025-04-28","description":"Marisa Meltzer's new book,This Is Big, chronicles the life of Jean Nidetch, the woman who founded Weight Watchers in 1963 and reflects on her own diet journey that began as a child.","tags":[]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"zokyrw","at":1778088457616},"key":"Clippings/Be lean with Jean How a housewife from Queens founded Weight Watchers.md"},
